  "overview": "**Visa Product Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#fcc015` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `visa-font-semi-bold` with `visa-font-regular` body copy (69px display down to 18px body), unified by `0px` razor-sharp architectural corners and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Visa**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://design.visa.com/welcome/). Inventory: **45** colors, **50** typography steps, and **27** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 27 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#ffffff` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 2px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, .2)`, `0 2px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, .2),inset 0 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#fcc015` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#fcc015` with `#0b0b0c` text (11.9:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `visa-font-semi-bold` headings with `visa-font-regular` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Enforce `0px` border-radius consistently across cards, inputs, and primary buttons.\n- Separate containers via `#ffffff` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not apply rounded corners (> 0px) to structural containers or CTA buttons.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
